/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_FixedMatrix FixedMatrix
 * @ingroup Foundation_Math
 *
 * @brief Fixed-size matrix container.
 *
 * The FixedMatrix class provides a statically allocated matrix whose
 * dimensions are known at compile time.
 *
 * Unlike dynamically allocated matrices, all storage is embedded directly
 * within the object:
 *
 * @code
 * FixedMatrix<float, 3, 3> matrix;
 * @endcode
 *
 * This design avoids heap allocation and provides deterministic memory
 * usage, making it suitable for embedded systems and real-time
 * applications.
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixFeatures Features
 *
 * - Compile-time dimensions.
 * - No dynamic memory allocation.
 * - Direct element access.
 * - Matrix addition and subtraction.
 * - Scalar multiplication and division.
 * - Matrix transposition.
 * - Compatible with generic numeric types.
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixLayout Memory Layout
 *
 * Elements are stored internally as:
 *
 * @code
 * T data[Rows][Cols];
 * @endcode
 *
 * in row-major order.
 *
 * Example:
 *
 * @code
 * [ a00 a01 a02 ]
 * [ a10 a11 a12 ]
 * [ a20 a21 a22 ]
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixConstruction Construction
 *
 * Default construction:
 *
 * @code
 * FixedMatrix<float, 2, 2> A;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Fill construction:
 *
 * @code
 * FixedMatrix<float, 2, 2> A(1.0f);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Array initialization:
 *
 * @code
 * float values[2][2] =
 * {
 *     {1.0f, 2.0f},
 *     {3.0f, 4.0f}
 * };
 *
 * FixedMatrix<float, 2, 2> A(values);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixElementAccess Element Access
 *
 * Access using At():
 *
 * @code
 * float value = matrix.At(1, 2);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Access using operator[]:
 *
 * @code
 * matrix[1][2] = 42.0f;
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixArithmetic Arithmetic Operations
 *
 * Matrix addition:
 *
 * @code
 * auto C = A + B;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Matrix subtraction:
 *
 * @code
 * auto C = A - B;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Scalar multiplication:
 *
 * @code
 * auto B = A * 2.0f;
 * auto C = 2.0f * A;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Scalar division:
 *
 * @code
 * auto B = A / 2.0f;
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixTranspose Transpose
 *
 * The transpose operation exchanges rows and columns:
 *
 * 
::contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}

 *
 * @code
 * FixedMatrix<float, 2, 3> A;
 *
 * auto AT = A.Transposed();
 *
 * // Result type:
 * // FixedMatrix<float, 3, 2>
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationFixedMatrixApplications Applications
 *
 * Typical applications include:
 *
 * - Coordinate transformations.
 * - DSP processing.
 * - Control systems.
 * - State-space models.
 * - Robotics kinematics.
 * - Embedded numerical algorithms.
 *
 * @see Foundation::Math::FixedMatrix
 */